# FBBNL-LABEL: name:            far_fbb_non_layout_tbb
# Analyzed TBB %bb.2 is near but NOT layout-next (trap %bb.1 sits between
# entry and near in layout). Far FBB %bb.3 -> only the trailing uncond is
# replaced; original BEQZ polarity retained; trap never branched to.
# FBBNL: bb.0.entry
# FBBNL: $r6 = LUI{{.*}}%bb.3{{$}}
# FBBNL: ADDI32{{.*}}%bb.3{{$}}
# FBBNL-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}} $r7
# FBBNL: BEQZ{{.*}} $r7, %bb.2,
# FBBNL-NOT: BNEZ
# FBBNL-NOT: B %bb.
# FBBNL: JALR
# FBBNL-NOT: B %bb.
# FBBNL: bb.1.trap
#
# ONEWAY-LABEL: name:            one_way_far_tbb
# One-way cond to far TBB: no trailing uncond exists, so the law names
# NO erasable member and the erase step is skipped entirely (one-way
# arm: append JALR only). The cond is inverted in place to the proven
# layout-successor near dest (BranchRelaxation.cpp:520-530 one-way
# fallthrough shape) and JALR takes the far edge.
# ONEWAY: bb.0.entry
# ONEWAY: $r6 = LUI{{.*}}%bb.2{{$}}
# ONEWAY: ADDI32{{.*}}%bb.2{{$}}
# ONEWAY-NOT: BEQZ{{.*}} $r7
# ONEWAY: BNEZ{{.*}} $r7, %bb.1,
# ONEWAY-NOT: B %bb.
# ONEWAY: JALR
# ONEWAY-NOT: B %bb.
# ONEWAY: bb.1.near
#
# MCLAW-LABEL: name:            multi_control_far_uncond
# The law names only the trailing uncond member of the coissued cycle:
# both retained conds and the ALU sibling survive; ALU is spliced before
# the first control; LUI/ADDI before that; JALR last; no leftover B.
# MCLAW: bb.0.entry
# MCLAW: $r3 = ADD32{{.*}} $r1, $r2
# MCLAW-NOT: B %bb.
# MCLAW: LUI{{.*}}%bb.2{{$}}
# MCLAW: ADDI32{{.*}}%bb.2{{$}}
# MCLAW: BEQZ{{.*}} $r4, %bb.1,
# MCLAW: BEQZ{{.*}} $r5, %bb.1,
# MCLAW-NOT: B %bb.
# MCLAW: JALR
# MCLAW-NOT: B %bb.
# MCLAW: bb.1.near

#--- corrupt.mir
--- |
  define dso_local void @two_uncond_cycles_corrupt() {
  entry:
    br i1 undef, label %near, label %far
  near:
    br label %far
  far:
    ret void
  }
...
