# Two unconditional control cycles in one tail is a corruption
# description: the law must refuse to name a selected member and (with
# the postcommit stamp armed by the finalize run) fail with the named
# ordered-terminator violation — never erase an unnamed member. The
# postcommit fatal aborts before any MIR print, so the pin is the named
# violation on stderr (function and block named), not a body LABEL.
# CORRUPT: ordered terminator tail: multiple unconditional control cycles in tail
